---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_20",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 20,
  "text": "<p> [[58.11]] <b>18. LEIBNIZ AN JOHANN GEORG GRAEVIUS</p>\n<p> [[58.12]] Frankfurt, 6./16. April 1670. [44a.]</b></p>\n<p> [[59.9]] Illustris et Amplissime Domine. </p>\n<p> [[59.10]] Cum non ita pridem ad doctissimum virum Joh. Henr. Horbium de cogitatis quibusdam\n[[59.11]] meis ad jurisprudentiam pertinentibus nonnulla perscripsissem, atque is Tibi ea, nescio quam\n[[59.12]] consulta rerum mearum fiducia, fortasse monstrasset; supra spem meam evenit, quod scripsit,\n[[59.13]] Tibi nimirum neque ingrata fuisse, neque prorsus contemnenda visa esse. Hoc ego nuncio\n[[59.14]] accepto nihil differendam putavi grati animi significationem, ac nisi Tu aliter judicas, satis\n[[59.15]] etiam excusatam hanc scribendi audaciam puto. </p>\n<p> [[59.16]] Quod ad rem ipsam attinet, animus est Ampl^#'m^#'o Lassero Consiliario Moguntino mihique,\n[[59.17]] tentare quousque in Jurisprudentia Rationali profici possit, ita tamen ut nihil conjecturarum\n[[59.18]] immisceatur. Hoc igitur velut exploratum sumsimus, certas quasdam haberi posse atque habendas\n[[59.19]] esse Juris naturalis demonstrationes, quibus stetur, quotiescunque <b>manifesta</b> non est facta\n[[59.20]] legibus mutatio. Has autem demonstrationes non erravero si dixerim hactenus nusquam\n[[59.21]] haberi. Equidem data est a me diligenter opera, ut legerem, quicquid fere ab excitatioribus\n[[59.22]] ingeniis in hoc argumento scriptum est. </p>\n<p> [[59.23]] Apud <b>Grotium</b>, cui quidem summae doctrinae atque omnigenae lectionis laudem nemo\n[[59.24]] sanus adimat, paucissima ex veris certa reddita sunt, falsa vero prorsus et multa et magna. Et\n[[59.25]] deprehendi, amore quodam libertatis, captata ab JC^#'t^#'i^#'s Romanis, aequitatis quadam specie,\n[[59.26]] dissentiendi occasione, saepe intima naturalis Jurisprudentiae adyta turbata esse, ut cum juris\n[[59.27]] realis personalisque discrimen, quantum in se erat, effectu sustulit, cum pacta nuda naturali jure\n[[59.28]] actionem parere posuit, cum contractuum bonae fidei et stricti juris differentias subvertit, quae\n[[59.29]] tamen a JC^#'t^#'i^#'s Romanis summa ratione recepta, a Francisco Connano aliisque rectissime defensa\n[[59.30]] sunt. Utinam vero Thomas <b>Hobbes</b> subtilitate sua pene divina in durissimas sententias abusus\n[[59.31]] non esset! Poteramus magna laboris parte levari, sed dum ille mira calliditate simul omnia et\n[[59.32]] dat et adimit Reipublicae, et nulla vitae sequentis cura, licentiam, si apud homines latere speres,\n[[59.33]] quidvis agendi relinquit, abstinendum fuit nobis a sententiis in sola Nusquamia Atheorum\n[[60.1]] valituris. <i>De</i> <b>Sharrokii</b> <i>Officiis</i>, <i>de</b> <b>Pallavicini</b> <i>Bono</i>, <i>de</b> <b>Thomae Angli</b> <i>Statera</i>, <i>de</b>\n[[60.2]] <b>Ivonis Parisini</b> <i>Jure naturali</i>, de <b>Caramuelis</b> meditationibus ut ipse vocat audacibus,\n[[60.3]] dicere hujus loci non est, nisi hoc unum, nullum eorum ejus quod justum est, scientiam\n[[60.4]] condidisse aut etiam mediocriter adumbrasse. </p>\n<p> [[60.5]] Ita nobis ipsa primum Elementa constituendi difficillimus labor relictus est, spero tamen\n[[60.6]] effecturos nos, si ita Deo visum erit, quod animo concepimus, ut Elementorum ejusmodi\n[[60.7]] propositio nulla, indemonstrata assumatur, demonstrationes autem omnes perpetua quadam\n[[60.8]] atque inviolabili Soritarum Catena firmatae, non animum magis quam oculos convincant. Porro\n[[60.9]] quae est Juris Romani ad Naturale ratio, ea juris localis ad Romanum, quando plerumque\n[[60.10]] receptum est ut statutis tacentibus juri Romano stetur. Pariter igitur illud inter prima artis\n[[60.11]] judicandi fundamenta ponendum est: quotiescunque lex Reipublicae de qua quaeritur quaestionem\n[[60.12]] propositam diserte non definit, toties quasi nulla lege extante recurrendum esse ad\n[[60.13]] indubitabilem normam juris naturalis, quod consultorem suum nunquam sine responso dimittit.\n[[60.14]] Juris Romani autem pars multo maxima prorsus naturalis est. Reliqua quae arbitraria sunt,\n[[60.15]] tametsi verbis multiplicata, sensu ac vi ipsa non ita vasta atque immania sunt, ut videntur.\n[[60.16]] Pleraeque enim leges, etiam quae praeter naturalem rationem aliquid continent, corollaria sunt\n[[60.17]] potius juris constituti, quam constitutrices novi. Adeo ut res in arctum satis compingi posse\n[[60.18]] videatur, si brevi quadam tabula ea omnia exhibeantur, quae neque ex naturali ratione, neque\n[[60.19]] alia lege pendent. Haec enim pauca et solvendis omnibus quaestionibus, et reddendis omnium\n[[60.20]] legum rationibus, addito naturali jure, sunt suffectura. Ex his derivare, in haec digerere leges\n[[60.21]] Romanas universas, id vero est, quod nos potissimum agitare profitemur. </p>\n<p> [[60.22]] Atque haec de Consilio nostro, cui ut faveas, Vir magne, si meretur, ut fautores, ut\n[[60.23]] adjumenta suppeditare ne negligas, etiam atque etiam rogo. Si quid vicissim jubes, quod in mea\n[[60.24]] potestate est, factum puta. </p>\n<p> [[60.25]] Profundiores Literas pudendum per Germaniam frigus occupavit. Intellexi tamen Reinesianorum\n[[60.26]] postumorum editionem in se recepisse Cl^#'m^#'u^#'m Bosium, ac praeter <i>inscriptiones</i>, ejus\n[[60.27]] additiones ad Vossium <i>de Historicis Graecis</i>, Onomasticon inscriptionum, Collectanea de\n[[60.28]] glossis seu verbis peregrinis, observationum in scriptoribus sacris ac profanis ac speciatim\n[[61.1]] medicis miscellanea, annotationes ad Patinum <i>de familiis Romanis</i>, Epistolarumque multas\n[[61.2]] Centurias expectari. Et eduntur nunc quas ad Daumium dedit, cum nonnullorum aliorum\n[[61.3]] specimine. </p>\n<p> [[61.4]] <i>Josephus</i> Bosii in eo est, ut prodeat. Nicolaus Schaten S.J. jussu principis <i>monumenta\n[[61.5]] Paderbornensia</i> edidit, credo optima quaeque operis ipsi principi deberi. Balbinus S.J. <i>Historiam\n[[61.6]] Bohemicam</i> Archi-­Episcopi Pragensis autoritate atque auspiciis molitur, qui literis\n[[61.7]] circularibus suffraganeos suos ad symbolam monumentorum conferendam hortatus est. Ericus\n[[61.8]] Mauritius invenit compilationem Feudorum Antonii de Prato Veteri Goldasto et Rigaltio frustra\n[[61.9]] quaesitam, Cuspiniano potissimum memoratam, quam jussu Friderici III. imperatoris Bononiensis\n[[61.10]] Academiae nomine confecit. Ordo ejus plane alius est a vulgari vel etiam Haloandrina\n[[61.11]] aut Cujaciana Feudorum editione, multaque magni momenti, alia aliterve, quam hactenus\n[[61.12]] prostant, ibi ut ajunt continentur. Sed quid ego Tibi aut notissima, aut parum digna scribo. Vale\n[[61.13]] faveque, </p>\n<p> [[61.14]] Vir Magne Cultori Tuo Gottfredo Guilielmo Leibnitio </p>\n<p> [[61.15]] Francof. 6/16 April. 1670. J.U.D. </p>\n<p> [[61.16]] P. S. Si rescribere dignaris, operculum literarum dirigi potest Moguntiam ad Ill^#'m^#'u^#'m Bar.\n[[61.17]] <b>Boineburgium</b> et maximis negotiis, et incredibili eruditione notissimum, qui Te magni facit,\n[[61.18]] atque etiam meis verbis salvere jubet. </p>\n",
  "number": "18.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN JOHANN GEORG GRAEVIUS",
  "date": "Frankfurt, 6./16. April 1670. [44a.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:18. LEIBNIZ AN JOHANN GEORG GRAEVIUS Frankfurt, 6./16. April 1670. [44a.] Illustris et Amplissime Domine. Cum non ita pridem ad doctissimum virum Joh. Henr. Horbium de cogitatis quibusdam meis ad jurisprudentiam pertinentibus nonnulla perscripsissem, atque is Tibi ea, nescio quam consulta rerum mear...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>